WEBVTT

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:07.080
Yui-san, regarding what you said earlier...

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.340
Does that mean you have your memories back?

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:15.450
I won't press you, then.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:20.610
Um...

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:22.620
I have a favor to ask you.

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:24.290
What might that be?

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:29.890
Would you mind not telling
the others about this just yet?

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:36.960
Come to think of it,

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:40.010
does that thing appear outside the academy and stuff, too?

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:40.920
That thing?

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:42.230
Oh, the ghost?

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:42.770
What?!

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:45.430
Oh! The Japanese ghost?

00:00:45.430 --> 00:00:49.640
I haven't heard of anyone seeing it
outside the academy so far.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:52.650
But there's something fishy about it.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.490
No, not necessarily.

00:00:55.490 --> 00:00:56.770
It could be here right now—

00:00:56.770 --> 00:00:58.160
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.700
Shall we be off?

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:01.910
What's the matter?

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:04.660
Oh, uh... Nothing.

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:05.940
Getting in some physical bonding.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:06.960
No.

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:10.320
Why now, after all this time?

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:13.570
My attendance!

00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:28.240
Have a great day!

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:29.680
See you!

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:35.280
Sleepy.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:37.940
The light was on in your room all last night.

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:39.320
Gaming again?

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:41.030
I couldn't find a good place to stop.

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:42.840
You shouldn't go so overboard.

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:46.070
But I'm never late to school,
so I'm better than <i>someone</i>, at least.

00:03:46.070 --> 00:03:47.330
And who might that be?

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:49.310
You're actually on time today?!

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:50.830
Morning, Airi-chan.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:51.060
You're actually on time today?!

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:52.080
How rude.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:53.330
Morning.

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:55.590
I'm on thin ice with my attendance already.

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:57.800
Plus, I got a warning from my
homeroom teacher the other day.

00:03:57.800 --> 00:03:59.000
Airi...

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:00.900
To think you'll be repeating
the year, all on your own...

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:04.380
And you get the best grades of any of us, too.

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:08.640
I told you, that's why I made sure not to be late today.

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:16.310
Airi-chan?

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:18.110
Oh, yeah...

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:27.410
Sou-kun, it's a little twisted.

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:30.040
Hey, stop that!

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:33.840
Sheesh! This is why people
call you sloppy, you know.

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:35.190
What?

00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:36.660
No, nothing.

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:40.230
Oh, and we're having a meeting at lunch about
the whole ghost thing, so everyone needs to come.

00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:41.880
See you there!

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:50.900
<i>That's...</i>

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:51.980
<i>Yui...</i>

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:54.420
<i>I wonder if she'll be okay.</i>

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:56.850
<i>She seems even less steady than Kaori.</i>

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:02.880
<i>Come to think of it...</i>

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:06.990
<i>The first time I ever talked to Kaori was during P.E. too, wasn't it?</i>

00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:17.360
Y-You're amazing, Hasekura-san.

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:19.890
You're not breathing hard at all.

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:21.970
Sasaki-san...

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:26.240
<i>Back then, I had my walls up pretty high,</i>

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:28.160
<i>so I probably wasn't easy to talk to.</i>

00:05:31.340 --> 00:05:34.520
<i>Ever since I was little,
I never really had a hard time with anything.</i>

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:37.140
<i>I ended up successful at anything I tried my hand at.</i>

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:42.570
<i>I liked the praise, so I kept
turning in good performances, but...</i>

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:45.790
<i>Around when I got into middle school,</i>

00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:49.870
<i>there was a part of me that
started feeling guilty about it.</i>

00:05:50.980 --> 00:05:53.750
<i>I became careful about not
giving things my best effort</i>

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:57.660
<i>and because of that, I couldn't really fit in.</i>

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:02.180
<i>And it was around then that
Kaori struck up a conversation with me.</i>

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:07.260
You were amazing at last year's
sports fest, Hasekura-san!

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:09.840
You left everyone in the dust during the relay!

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:11.830
I was so impressed watching you.

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:13.640
I'm really bad at running, you see.

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:15.480
Right...

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:19.280
Okay! Next up, you'll split up
into teams to run a relay race.

00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:21.600
The team that comes in last
will be doing track maintenance.

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:22.900
What?!

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:26.800
Running makes me nervous.

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:28.200
Let's do our best!

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:28.600
Sure...

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:30.120
I haven't done this in ages!

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:32.070
If we're on the same team as Kaori...

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:34.580
We'd better prepare to lose.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:55.920
Figured as much.

00:06:55.920 --> 00:06:57.340
Aw, man.

00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:13.370
Hasekura-san!

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:19.460
No way!

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:20.330
Wow!

00:07:36.790 --> 00:07:38.680
That was amazing, Hasekura-san!

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:40.560
You passed them all!

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:42.390
Awesome! That was so cool!

00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:44.560
<i>I have to admit, I'm a simple creature.</i>

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:47.110
<i>Getting to see Kaori smile like that</i>

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:50.000
<i>made me stop caring about
what others thought of me.</i>

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:09.860
<i>Wow, I didn't see that coming.</i>

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:16.200
Got it, everyone?

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:19.260
We're doing a thorough investigation after school today!

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:22.190
Thank you for the food.

00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:23.700
Please, Sou!

00:08:23.700 --> 00:08:26.230
Won't you share that obviously tasty-looking lunch with me?

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:27.600
You just ate earlier.

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:28.650
Hey, are you listening?!

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:30.160
We are.

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:33.110
By the way, why are we on the roof
instead of in the club room?

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:34.610
The weather's too good to waste.

00:08:35.560 --> 00:08:37.740
Stupid question, I guess.

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:39.030
The ghost, huh?

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:40.070
I'm not looking forward to that.

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:43.080
S-Someone! Someone, feed me lunch!

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:46.050
At this rate, I won't have
any energy for after school!

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:46.660
No!

00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:49.640
Cut the racket. You can just go buy something, right?

00:08:49.640 --> 00:08:51.750
Oh, good idea!

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:52.980
I'm off!

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:54.220
Lunch!

00:08:55.370 --> 00:08:57.720
We're down one now. You fine with that?

00:08:57.720 --> 00:08:59.400
Is there a problem?

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:00.220
Guess not.

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:02.740
Yui-san, aren't you going to eat?

00:09:02.740 --> 00:09:05.330
Oh, yes. I will be eating.

00:09:05.330 --> 00:09:08.550
That reminds me. I saw you in P.E. earlier,

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:09.860
running hurdles.

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:11.890
You're actually pretty athletic, huh?

00:09:11.890 --> 00:09:15.860
Once you learn how, the rest is just repetition.

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:17.750
Well, true.

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:20.740
Furukawa, is it just me or do you seem like a different person?

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:21.740
What?

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:23.600
You kind of sound like Airi-chan.

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:24.550
Me?

00:09:24.550 --> 00:09:26.520
The way she phrases things is different,

00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:29.670
but I thought it seemed like
the sort of thing you'd say.

00:09:32.450 --> 00:09:34.880
You think? They seem totally different to me.

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:40.160
Oh, no! Mistake!

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:42.290
I realized I have no money on me!

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:44.290
It's business as usual with Kenny.

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:48.650
Kenny-kun, you can have
some of my lunch if you'd like.

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:51.650
Kaori-chan, you're like an angel!

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:54.130
Don't, Kaori. Don't spoil him.

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:55.250
He'll start to expect it.

00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:58.110
As a dog owner, your responsibilities include proper discipline.

00:09:58.110 --> 00:09:59.890
Everyone's being so cold to me...

00:09:59.890 --> 00:10:01.950
Jennifer!

00:10:09.320 --> 00:10:10.920
Ooh!

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:16.500
All right, everyone! We're springing into action!

00:10:16.500 --> 00:10:18.880
Based on the eyewitness accounts that we've compiled...

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:20.240
Hasekura-san!

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:24.010
The Judo Club and the Karate Club?

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:26.370
The situation is highly volatile!

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:28.210
If things go bad, this could be a major disaster!

00:10:28.210 --> 00:10:30.740
Do something about those barbarians!

00:10:30.740 --> 00:10:33.170
I am not against rough behavior,

00:10:33.170 --> 00:10:35.700
but you would do well to calm down a little.

00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:37.110
Never mind that! Get going already!

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:39.750
That's what the Astronomy Club is for, right?!

00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:42.870
Uh, last time I checked it was for astronomy.

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:46.390
Well, we accepted the duty of subduing any trouble that arose from the school festival,

00:10:46.390 --> 00:10:49.000
so this counts as a club activity as well.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:51.800
You say that, but it looks like you're having fun, Prez.

00:10:51.800 --> 00:10:52.880
Can you tell?

00:10:53.370 --> 00:10:55.630
Then I'll hold the fort here.

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:56.790
Didn't you hear me?

00:10:56.790 --> 00:10:58.880
This is an important club activity in its own right.

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:04.110
Just give in, Sou-san.

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:12.420
The Judo Club...

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:14.690
An ankle injury...

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:16.440
I can't wait to take them on!

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:18.090
Woohoo!

00:11:18.090 --> 00:11:21.010
I'm just a normal human being, you know.

00:11:21.010 --> 00:11:23.240
No point griping now, Sou-kun.

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:30.500
You mustn't, Sasaki-san! It's dangerous!

00:11:31.610 --> 00:11:32.930
Furukawa-san?

00:11:40.940 --> 00:11:42.010
What's wrong?

00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:46.890
It'll be okay.

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:51.000
I'll only step in to stop them
when they get too carried away.

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:51.920
But...

00:11:53.240 --> 00:11:56.630
I'm a member of the Astronomy Club too.

00:11:56.630 --> 00:11:57.650
I have to go.

00:12:05.560 --> 00:12:07.410
This is so dumb I can barely
keep from rolling my eyes.

00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:10.150
Aren't you guys embarrassed,

00:12:10.150 --> 00:12:13.920
taking advantage of the fact that the Karate Club
can't touch you because they take their club seriously?

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:16.580
Serious, my ass!

00:12:16.580 --> 00:12:18.660
They're the pitiful ones who got bribed by Sasaki Kaori

00:12:18.660 --> 00:12:22.510
to give up some of their demo time
at the school festival!

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:23.080
Sasaki-san has nothing to do with this!

00:12:23.080 --> 00:12:24.820
There they are, going at it.

00:12:24.820 --> 00:12:26.530
That's right. How dare you put it like that?

00:12:26.530 --> 00:12:29.090
That was a negotiation, not a bribe.

00:12:29.090 --> 00:12:30.520
Same difference, right?!

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:33.400
Oh? Speak of the devil.

00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:35.400
You're the one who bribed them, right?

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:36.580
Hey!

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:39.510
C'mon, calm down!

00:12:39.510 --> 00:12:41.400
I gave them that to thank them!

00:12:41.750 --> 00:12:42.400
Please take back what you...

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:44.120
Sasaki-san, this way.

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:45.910
Huh? What? Huh?

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:51.200
Wh-What's your problem?
You her knight in shining armor?

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:51.660
What?

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:53.620
No, um...

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:54.660
Uh-oh...

00:12:57.670 --> 00:12:58.140
W-Wait!

00:12:58.140 --> 00:13:01.010
<i>If Sasaki-san avoids getting injured now...</i>

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:11.940
Sou!

00:13:11.940 --> 00:13:13.060
Get outta my way!

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:14.820
Sou-kun!

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:22.450
You better be ready for what's coming!

00:13:29.360 --> 00:13:30.640
Sou...

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:33.910
The Prez and I avenged you.

00:13:33.910 --> 00:13:35.560
Don't talk like I'm dead!

00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:36.240
Owowow!

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:37.670
A-Are you okay?

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:39.040
It's no big deal.

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:40.310
Sou, you idiot.

00:13:40.310 --> 00:13:42.160
That's what you get for trying
to be a hero when you're weak.

00:13:42.160 --> 00:13:45.030
I'll have you know it's not me that's weak.

00:13:45.030 --> 00:13:48.180
<i>You</i> guys are the anomalies
for being able to crush the Judo Club.

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:52.060
I'm sorry, Sou-kun. It's my fault.

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:53.220
Kaori...

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:55.640
That isn't true.

00:13:58.140 --> 00:14:00.740
It is likely my fault.

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:04.400
Akiyama-sun got hurt because of me.

00:14:05.130 --> 00:14:06.000
Yui?

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:09.920
Oh, no. No one thinks it's your fault.

00:14:09.920 --> 00:14:12.370
It's my bad for being dumb enough to let myself get dragged into it.

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:14.280
I agree with Sou-san.

00:14:14.280 --> 00:14:18.370
Earlier, the members of the Judo Club also acknowledged that they were in the wrong.
Yeah...

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:20.380
Hanamiya-senpai...

00:14:20.680 --> 00:14:24.180
Let us leave the rest to the teachers and the student council.

00:14:24.180 --> 00:14:26.320
Nice backup, Nagisa-kun.

00:14:26.320 --> 00:14:30.560
This doesn't seem like the time to go
investigating ghosts anymore, does it?

00:14:30.560 --> 00:14:33.510
Kaori, just take Sou for today and...

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:34.430
Sou?

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:38.350
I told you, didn't I? It's no big deal at all.

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:41.180
There's still time, so let's start the investigation.

00:14:42.270 --> 00:14:44.350
Okay! Let's go!

00:14:51.350 --> 00:14:53.040
It actually hurts, right?

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:53.870
Nope.

00:14:54.430 --> 00:14:56.980
But it <i>actually</i> hurts, right?

00:14:57.940 --> 00:14:58.580
Yeah...

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:01.080
Owowow...

00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:03.990
Whenever I see that look on her face...

00:15:03.990 --> 00:15:06.170
Well, I've never been good at handling it.

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:07.600
I know.

00:15:13.630 --> 00:15:16.660
In spite of everything,
I guess Sou-san is still a guy, after all.

00:15:16.660 --> 00:15:17.140
What?

00:15:17.140 --> 00:15:19.970
Don't mind me. I was just talking to myself.

00:15:19.970 --> 00:15:23.860
By the way, Nagisa-kun,
why are we going to the library?

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:25.600
We're going to go question someone.

00:15:25.600 --> 00:15:29.360
Are you familiar with the phrase
"human encyclopedia"?

00:15:32.320 --> 00:15:35.740
I wonder if Sou-kun's really all right.

00:15:36.070 --> 00:15:40.020
Because I interfered, Akiyama-san was injured.

00:15:43.460 --> 00:15:47.440
The more I take action,
the more unpredictable things happen.

00:15:48.810 --> 00:15:50.100
Furukawa-san?

00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:58.000
Are you aware of the ghost that the
students are all talking about lately?

00:15:58.000 --> 00:16:00.500
Oh, to some extent.

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:03.770
Does it ring any bells?

00:16:03.770 --> 00:16:05.160
For example,

00:16:05.160 --> 00:16:08.020
perhaps there was some incident that happened at this school in the past?

00:16:10.670 --> 00:16:13.030
I don't know of anything like that, but...

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:16.100
I happened to see that ghost myself the other day.

00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:17.280
Really?!

00:16:17.730 --> 00:16:22.610
She was really faint, but I saw her sitting on the bench on the roof.

00:16:22.610 --> 00:16:25.520
It was right around this time of day.

00:16:25.520 --> 00:16:26.780
The roof...

00:16:30.230 --> 00:16:32.840
If so, maybe it would be better to do nothing at all.

00:16:32.840 --> 00:16:34.370
Is something wrong?

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:38.210
But in that case, I...

00:16:39.840 --> 00:16:45.180
Sasaki-san?

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:58.000
How is it?

00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:00.030
My body still feels creaky.

00:17:00.310 --> 00:17:03.560
You should at least work out to the point
where you can protect Kaori.

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:05.300
I won't expect you to reach Kenny's level, though.

00:17:05.300 --> 00:17:07.360
As if I could become a monster like him!

00:17:07.840 --> 00:17:10.240
But maybe I <i>will</i> work out a little.

00:17:10.240 --> 00:17:11.550
Yeah...

00:17:12.440 --> 00:17:14.460
Hey, do you remember?

00:17:15.310 --> 00:17:17.800
About the day you first met me.

00:17:18.100 --> 00:17:20.100
Like I could ever forget.

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:20.740
What?

00:17:20.740 --> 00:17:23.600
We'd only just met, and you suddenly
kicked the hell out of me.

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:26.500
Wait, why did I get kicked again?

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:27.810
Th-That was because you...

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:31.700
Oh, hello. I'm Akiyama.

00:17:34.430 --> 00:17:36.930
Your eyes are strong and beautiful!

00:17:36.930 --> 00:17:38.660
Your face is cute too, of course, but...

00:17:42.560 --> 00:17:43.160
Ow!

00:17:43.760 --> 00:17:46.640
Can you blame me?
You said all this weird stuff out of the blue.

00:17:46.640 --> 00:17:48.070
What did I say again?

00:17:48.070 --> 00:17:50.920
If you don't remember, then that's fine.

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:54.170
It's like we haven't changed at all.

00:17:55.550 --> 00:17:57.170
That's not true.

00:17:59.880 --> 00:18:00.830
Airi?

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:02.930
Kaori!

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:04.420
Did it appear? The ghost?

00:18:06.160 --> 00:18:09.150
Gho... It... I-It... It...

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:12.110
I-It... Gh-Gho...

00:18:12.470 --> 00:18:13.320
Kaori-san!

00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:14.780
What happened?

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:16.630
Ca... C-C-Ca...

00:18:16.630 --> 00:18:17.890
Cafeteria...

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:19.490
Okay!

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:21.650
Japanese ghost! Lock on!

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:25.000
Are you two okay?

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:26.230
Y-Yeah.

00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:28.080
I am okay too.

00:18:28.560 --> 00:18:30.720
The cafeteria, was it? Want to go check it out?

00:18:30.720 --> 00:18:31.890
N-No, no, no, no!

00:18:31.890 --> 00:18:32.850
N-No, thank you!

00:18:32.850 --> 00:18:34.420
I'll stay right here!

00:18:34.420 --> 00:18:36.580
You didn't wet yourself again, did you?

00:18:36.580 --> 00:18:38.640
Wh-What are you talking about, Sou-kun?!

00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:40.470
So you have wet yourself before?

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:48.160
It's the Astronomy Club!

00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:48.960
Crap!

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:50.590
If we get caught, we'll have hell to pay!

00:18:52.850 --> 00:18:55.250
Stop right there!

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:01.920
P-Prez...

00:19:03.630 --> 00:19:05.370
You guys...

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:08.040
You're with the Film Society, if I remember correctly.

00:19:21.970 --> 00:19:23.940
A horror workshop?

00:19:23.940 --> 00:19:24.720
Yeah.

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:28.710
So you were filming it to serve as an
attraction during the school festival?

00:19:28.710 --> 00:19:31.730
We wanted to test what kind of reaction we'd get.

00:19:32.050 --> 00:19:36.180
This version turned out pretty good,
and we were confident, so...

00:19:36.180 --> 00:19:38.770
We never thought it'd become such a big deal.

00:19:38.770 --> 00:19:40.320
Of course it would!

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:41.490
We're sorry!

00:19:52.230 --> 00:19:54.260
So, when the ghost was examined closely...

00:19:54.260 --> 00:19:55.650
Cauliflower.

00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:59.840
I suppose that solves the rash of ghost incidents, then?

00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:01.250
It looks that way.

00:20:01.250 --> 00:20:05.510
The student council will handle notifying the students later.

00:20:06.230 --> 00:20:07.760
We're sorry.

00:20:07.760 --> 00:20:11.160
Seriously, talk about making a mess.

00:20:11.160 --> 00:20:13.480
Then, Azuma Yaeko-san's report

00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:16.260
and the one Ogawa-sensei saw on the roof were also...

00:20:16.260 --> 00:20:16.770
Huh?

00:20:16.770 --> 00:20:20.020
You've got no business going around randomly scaring people!

00:20:20.020 --> 00:20:21.780
We're sorry!

00:20:28.890 --> 00:20:29.540
The roof?

00:20:30.010 --> 00:20:31.170
Was that one of ours?

00:20:31.170 --> 00:20:33.420
No, not that I'm aware of.

00:20:46.900 --> 00:20:50.840
Well, looks like the preparations for the
school festival should be smooth sailing now.

00:20:50.840 --> 00:20:53.860
Our own preparations are nowhere near done, though.

00:20:53.860 --> 00:20:56.270
This is where a little elbow grease on your end will work wonders.

00:20:56.270 --> 00:20:58.270
Don't talk like it isn't your problem too!

00:21:00.160 --> 00:21:01.960
Where did you get that?

00:21:01.960 --> 00:21:04.780
The Film Society members gave it to us as an apology.

00:21:04.780 --> 00:21:06.820
I saw Nagisa-kun shaking them down for that.

00:21:06.820 --> 00:21:07.660
A fee for our troubles.

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:11.000
By rights, it should go to you, Kaori-san.

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:12.660
Oh no, I couldn't.

00:21:12.660 --> 00:21:16.360
Then, Sou-san, you like this sort of thing, right?

00:21:16.360 --> 00:21:17.220
Yeah.

00:21:18.480 --> 00:21:19.390
Wow...

00:21:20.720 --> 00:21:23.480
Sou-kun, what about your injuries? Are you okay?

00:21:23.480 --> 00:21:25.260
Yeah, they're no big deal.

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:28.290
That's my partner for you!

00:21:28.290 --> 00:21:29.540
Spare me.

00:21:30.700 --> 00:21:32.970
Are you worried about Sou-san's injuries?

00:21:32.970 --> 00:21:33.680
What?

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:35.210
And <i>we</i> need to get moving on the café side of things.

00:21:35.210 --> 00:21:36.670
You seem to have something else
on your mind, though.

00:21:36.670 --> 00:21:39.400
What kinds of sweets should we put on the menu?

00:21:39.400 --> 00:21:42.180
I feel like we could sell anything
if we label it as homemade by Kaori.

00:21:42.180 --> 00:21:43.730
Yes! Prez, that's it!

00:21:43.730 --> 00:21:45.180
You two...

00:21:45.520 --> 00:21:49.640
You're going to make me build the planetarium and make Kaori bake the sweets...

00:23:26.880 --> 00:23:27.840
I think you should know better than to ask me.

00:23:27.840 --> 00:23:29.330
I think, "I have to make this moment count!"

00:23:29.330 --> 00:23:30.450
There's no turning back now.

00:23:30.450 --> 00:23:31.760
I have no need of memories.

00:23:31.760 --> 00:23:32.870
My heart's still pounding.

00:23:32.870 --> 00:23:34.220
Yeah! We have arrived!

00:23:34.220 --> 00:23:36.280
Oh, Yui-chan!

00:23:36.280 --> 00:23:39.740
Episode four: "All Things Are in a State of Flux."
